            "text": "{\n  \"relation\": \"NOVEL\",\n  \"consensus_summary\": \"The consensus identifies 'living creatures' primarily as the exalted angelic beings (cherubim) surrounding God's throne in Ezekiel and Revelation, with secondary symbolic traditions equating them to the four Evangelists, aspects of Christ, or the totality of animate creation. A nonsymbolic lexical sense applies to ordinary animals.\",\n  \"book_summary\": \"The book defines 'living creature' as a nation or people, drawing a parallel between the beasts of Daniel's sea and the creatures in Revelation's sea.\",\n  \"consensus_core_identification\": \"Angelic throne attendants (cherubim), the four Evangelists, or literal animals/animate creation.\",\n  \"book_core_identification\": \"A nation or people.\",\n  \"core_relation\": \"NO_CONSENSUS\",\n  \"extension_relation\": \"NO_BASELINE\",\n  \"boundary_disagreement\": \"The consensus focuses on the four heavenly living creatures (zōa) around the throne or the literal animals of Genesis. The book zeroes in on the creatures in the sea during the bowl and trumpet judgments (Rev 8:9, 16:3), interpreting them symbolically as nations or peoples.\",\n  \"material_contradiction\": \"The consensus interprets the 'creatures' in Revelation's sea plagues as literal marine life or general creation, whereas the book interprets them as a symbolic representation of nations and peoples.\",\n  \"rationale\": \"None of the consensus respondents list 'nation' or 'people' as a meaning for 'living creature', nor do they reference the sea creatures in Revelation 8 and 16 as a distinct symbolic category. The book's interpretation is therefore entirely novel compared to standard typologies.\",\n  \"citation_support\": \"PARTIAL\",\n  \"strongest_objection\": \"The text in Revelation 8:9 and 16:3 likely refers to literal marine life affected by the plagues, whereas the 'beasts' (thēria) in Daniel 7 are explicitly defined by the text as symbolic kings/kingdoms. Equating the generic Greek terms for living things in Revelation's sea to the specific symbolic beasts of Daniel is an exegetical leap.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\"\n}",
